cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jittest in research, please cite the underlying method (preferred-citation) as well as this software."
title: "jittest: an open-source implementation of Just-in-Time Catching Test generation"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kartik24Hulmukh/jittest"
abstract: >-
  jittest generates candidate unit tests for a code diff and keeps only those
  that pass on the base commit and fail on the head commit, verified by
  execution rather than by a language model. It is an independent community
  implementation of the Just-in-Time Catching Test method published by Meta,
  and a response to the Catching JiTTest Challenge posed at FSE 2025.
keywords:
  - software testing
  - test generation
  - regression testing
  - large language models
  - continuous integration
authors:
  - name: "jittest contributors"

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Just-in-Time Catching Test Generation at Meta"
  year: 2026
  journal: "arXiv preprint"
  url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22832"
  authors:
